 - **When Not to Use:** Spherical scenes, scenes with significant camera rotation around the object, or when exact world-space depth is required for other processing steps [S2, S6, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-General NDC Ray Conversion was introduced in the context of NeRF (Neural Radiance Fields) to handle forward-facing scenes efficiently. The technique maps the perspective frustum to a canonical cube, allowing for simpler and more robust sampling strategies. It is particularly useful for datasets like LLFF (Look at Light From the Front) where the camera moves primarily in a forward-facing manner [S4, S6, unofficial].
